The exact Na2seo3 successor 56b2ec00 and three-operation deferral bridge d4034703 pass this bounded independent review. No new finding was identified. This is a recommendation for these private artifacts, not authorization to apply a corrected campaign or admit its exports.

The complete owner retains CHEBI:48843, its disodium-selenite formula 2Na.O3Se, CAS 10102-18-8, structure, exact mapping, all valid aliases, occurrence statistics and inherited role fields. The captured official ChEBI record cfe139a3 supports the chemical identity, canonical label, formula, structure and CAS. Inverting the one synonym-type change and removing the one appended evidence/history pair reproduces the entire selected predecessor exactly. The supported `Na2SeO3 (anhydrous)` alias and its four source occurrences remain. Existing hidden-hydrate rejections and every historical event remain byte-for-byte in the parsed prefixes. No new whole-role, occurrence-quantity or export approval is supplied.

The new `REJECTED_LABEL` is supported as a restriction on this owner's resolving alias, not as a claim that the original reagent was a different chemical. DSMZ863 capture312943d4 literally prints `Na2Se2O3` at0.100g. Official MediaDive804 capturefd2c8ff3 retains the same name without a CAS, formula or ChEBI identifier. The independently supported owner's formula has one selenium atom, while that literal has two. These positive facts establish a literal identity mismatch requiring source-specific adjudication, rather than a legitimate global synonym. Current W01 case169 and #718 retain the unresolved reagent. Missing an erratum alone would not establish this conclusion; the literal/formula mismatch and documented scope hold are essential.

The historical `MERGED_FROM_UNMAPPED_DUPLICATE` event is preserved, including its Edison/MediaDive/OAK claim. Actual Git commit026d4401322be01c449ccf29bf04ad6842b56ba6 explicitly records Edison's caution, “don't exactMatch a malformed label,” and treats retaining RAW_TEXT as asserting no new exact mapping row. That historical reasoning makes the likely-typo interpretation understandable; it does not establish an identity-bearing global alias. The current native projection demonstrably exports that RAW_TEXT token as a synonym of CHEBI:48843. The successor corrects this resolver exposure without erasing the earlier inference or deciding the original reagent's identity. The raw Edison research report was not independently re-researched; this judgement relies on the inspected historical commit, current official captures and current source-case hold.

The new evidence is explicitly agent-authored LLM_SUGGESTION and the new history is LLM-assisted. It attaches to the narrow applicability claim. The source is the filed #718 comment6724233754. Fresh read-only captures of #718 and #1237 bodies/comments are included. The first network failure is retained separately; it was not interpreted as absence of an issue.

The actual-KG native differential changes only `source` and `other`; only `Na2Se2O3` is removed from the latter. A second native diagnostic deliberately reintroduces that token through the KG label list and confirms its exclusion still holds. The positive anhydrous alias, exact predicate, object, comment, confidence and method are retained. These are per-owner diagnostics using the actual KG gzip and authentic A842 mapped inventory with the exact candidate; no complete corrected-campaign generation, residual accounting, stamp replay or source application occurred.

The deferral bridge preserves all three original create/null-preimage operations, their complete proposal objects and all four source-case objects. It changes no source decision or occurrence, invents no replacement origin and declares no future plan hash/count. Original published W01 da45 core bytes and proposal/case joins were checked directly in Git; the Na edit preimage also matches authentic A842 committed bytes. Partial/cancelled B was never treated as an after-state. Frozen report payload captures are evidence, not evidence of completed application.

NBRC1257 and1321 each positively supply8.4g NaHCO3 plus100mL added distilled water, CO2 saturation and sealed autoclaving. Their shared source profile is supported. The maintained84g/L comparator's J451 official MediaDive capture7e4712df explicitly includes autoclaving under CO2. Omitted saturation details or different denominator notation establish neither a separate supplied stock nor equivalence. Deferring the additional owner while retaining the generic owner's separate original operation is justified pending continuity adjudication; the generic owner is not silently selected as an exact merge target.

NBRC1020 and JCM317 both print4mg selenite plus4mg tungstate and1L added water; JCM317 explicitly names tungstate dihydrate, while NBRC1020 leaves the form unqualified. That omission establishes neither a second distinct stock nor full identity with the explicit hydrate recipe. Deferring both creates preserves the actual co-installation condition and literal source profiles. No NBRC824 missing denominator is repaired, no water input is converted into measured final volume and no source number is treated as identity.

